# G6 acceptance gates — home domain + new overview landing (2026-09-14)

## Step 0: sales datasource audit (decision A taken)

- crm_deals columns: id,name,deadline,amount,status,owner,customer_id,stage,
  expected_close_date,closed_date; stage enum identical to hub_sales_deals
  (inquiry/quote/negotiation/won/lost) and `amount` shares the name+type.
- Mapping: hub_sales_deals→crm_deals (title→name, account append→customer),
  hub_sales_activities→crm_activities (subject→title), quick-search sources →
  crm_customers / crm_contacts / crm_deals / crm_leads. No fallback branch
  needed; every field the overview/week-strip consumes exists on crm_*.

## Recorded forks (intentional, vs frozen Hub source)

- pages/home/data.ts + quick-search.tsx: sales queries rebound per the
  mapping above; all other home files stay byte-identical to Hub.
- quick-search deep links remapped: /accounts/show→/customers/show,
  /deals/show→/pipeline/show (CRM route shapes), /contacts/show→/contacts
  (CRM has no contact detail route), /leads/show unchanged.
- pages/home/module.tsx: resource priority 0→-1 so the overview precedes the
  crm_nav_* groups and the root NavigateToAccessibleResource lands on
